WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:01.920
We have a voicemail number

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.920
That number is 219-2DAVIDP

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.460
This is a voicemail from someone we've been sort of speculating

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.380
what will ultimately

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.920
pull Trump's approval rating

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.120
really down further than the already record low numbers

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.240
that he's already experiencing

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.120
what will it take

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.900
for Republicians to say "we need Trump out".

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.280
Here's one caller

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:26.220
who had an idea about what it might take to ultimately turn those last

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.540
recalcitrant Trump supporters

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:29.380
against him.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:35.200
"...(David) the only way we'll be able to get rid of Donnie [Donald Trump] is if the economy tanks"

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.720
"I know everybody's gonna suffer if the economy tanks but..."

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:43.540
that's the item that will let people up to his terrible, terrible presidency"

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:44.740
Yeah

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.280
Uh, I don't agree

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.320
I don't agree because

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.540
even when the economy tanks

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:54.040
You'll have a really good propaganda campaign

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.340
about how well things are going

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:59.100
We see it under every administration

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.480
Every administration

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.440
Democratic and Republician

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:05.820
Will make the case that the economy is doing okay

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:07.980
and George W. Bush...recall

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.120
George W. Bush was re-elected

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:12.200
during...not good

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:13.620
...really not good

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:15.820
(uh) economic circumstances

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:19.100
and although I would like to agree with the caller

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:23.020
that...again, it's this idea of once it hits you personally,

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:24.420
you will change your mind

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.540
I would like to agree with the caller

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:29.360
that if Donald Trump does start to tank the economy

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:30.520
and how we define that

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:32.600
well...there's different ways we would define that

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.200
people would abandon Trump...

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.460
...I don't believe they would

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.440
because there will be a narrative

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:39.320
that would come from the Trump administration

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:43.240
that *will* resonate with some significant portion of Trump supporters

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:44.400
and sadly like I said before

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.100
even with a 30% approval rating

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:49.800
Donald...Donald Trump could still be re-elected President of the United States

